00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:48.470
Oh yeah. Yeah, it's just a...

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:51.470
False alarm. Probably a prank.

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:57.430
Happens all the time.

00:22:57.430 --> 00:23:00.430
Hey. That's blood.

00:23:00.430 --> 00:23:05.460
I need to go.

00:23:05.460 --> 00:23:06.460
Hold on.

00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:19.279
Marit Joseph.

00:23:19.279 --> 00:23:21.279
What the hell did you put in there?

00:23:21.279 --> 00:23:22.279
What did you put in there?

00:23:22.279 --> 00:23:23.279
What did you put in there?

00:23:23.279 --> 00:23:24.279
Did you do?

00:23:24.279 --> 00:23:25.279
Is that my fault?

00:23:25.279 --> 00:23:26.279
I blacked out.

00:23:26.279 --> 00:23:30.940
I couldn't control it.

00:23:30.940 --> 00:23:31.940
Okay.

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:32.940
Listen to me.

00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:34.940
You need to go right now.

00:23:34.940 --> 00:23:36.940
I'm not going anywhere.

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:39.940
You aren't either until the cops get here.

00:23:39.940 --> 00:24:09.339
Now we'd like to ask Chloe's escort to join her on the dance floor.

00:24:09.339 --> 00:24:10.339
Hey, Clark.

00:24:10.339 --> 00:24:13.339
It's time to boogie.

00:24:13.339 --> 00:24:21.779
I know what's weird, isn't it?

00:24:21.779 --> 00:24:22.779
A little.

00:24:22.779 --> 00:24:27.059
Thank you for letting us have our wedding here.

00:24:27.059 --> 00:24:30.069
I know.

00:24:30.069 --> 00:24:31.069
At least I can do.

00:24:31.069 --> 00:24:35.579
You're always the best friend I ever could have had.

00:24:35.579 --> 00:24:40.589
You say that like something's changed.

00:24:40.589 --> 00:24:42.589
Clark, trust me.

00:24:42.589 --> 00:24:43.589
We've been through too much together.

00:24:43.589 --> 00:24:52.769
Nothing is going to make me forget that.

00:24:52.769 --> 00:25:01.180
The important thing is that your life is everything you wanted to be.

00:25:01.180 --> 00:25:04.180
It's like I've been carrying around this weight.

00:25:04.180 --> 00:25:07.180
I don't know why, but a few days ago,

00:25:07.180 --> 00:25:09.779
only let go.

00:25:09.779 --> 00:25:13.059
Like I can move on.

00:25:13.059 --> 00:25:19.309
Okay, CK.

00:25:19.309 --> 00:25:38.819
I turn to dance for my wife.

00:25:38.819 --> 00:25:40.819
Guess I can give these well-heeled puppies a rest.

00:25:40.819 --> 00:27:39.039
You want a glass with that?

00:27:39.039 --> 00:27:40.039
Oliver.

00:27:40.039 --> 00:27:42.039
Just the person I want to see right now.

00:27:42.039 --> 00:27:47.039
So, um, tell me what started this lost weekend?

00:27:47.039 --> 00:27:49.039
Go and enjoy the party.

00:27:49.039 --> 00:27:53.039
Trust me, it'll be a real buzzkill to listen to me wine like Patsy Cline.

00:27:53.039 --> 00:27:56.039
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:27:56.039 --> 00:28:00.039
You know, um, I may not be at the top of your confidon list,

00:28:00.039 --> 00:28:02.039
but if you ever want to talk, I'm here.

00:28:02.039 --> 00:28:15.829
I'm just having all these feelings and I don't know what they mean.

00:28:15.829 --> 00:28:18.430
Oh.

00:28:18.430 --> 00:28:19.430
Who's the lucky guy?

00:28:19.430 --> 00:28:35.250
Having this conversation with an axe is bad enough without turning up the awkward dial.

00:28:35.250 --> 00:28:42.250
Well, you know, there's moving on in theory, and then there's the moment that it actually happens.

00:28:42.250 --> 00:28:46.250
If you'd like, we can start now, then I'll just be a really good friend.

00:28:46.250 --> 00:29:00.809
It's like I was going along and it just knuck up on me.

00:29:00.809 --> 00:29:07.140
And I try to ignore it, but then there are these moments.

00:29:07.140 --> 00:29:09.140
that you can't.

00:29:09.140 --> 00:29:16.140
Maybe I was reading it wrong.

00:29:16.140 --> 00:29:20.140
And to add insult to injury, it all went down at tonight's tribute to romantic bliss.

00:29:20.140 --> 00:29:36.460
I know it sounds sappy, but I thought,

00:29:36.460 --> 00:29:44.170
just for a minute, someone needed me.

00:29:44.170 --> 00:29:49.940
Well, I'm sure he needs you, Lois.

00:29:49.940 --> 00:29:55.500
That's sweet of you to say, but how do you know?

00:29:55.500 --> 00:29:59.809
Because I know Clark?

00:29:59.809 --> 00:30:41.269
Chloe's glad you came. I could have used some warning.

00:30:41.269 --> 00:30:52.559
You weren't planning on coming back, were you?

00:30:52.559 --> 00:30:53.559
Yeah, not until a few.

00:30:53.559 --> 00:30:54.559
few hours ago.

00:30:54.559 --> 00:31:12.339
So what changed your mind?

00:31:12.339 --> 00:31:19.200
I'm not expecting you to say it was me.

00:31:19.200 --> 00:31:22.200
I read about the mysterious blur saving lives in metropolis.

00:31:22.200 --> 00:31:25.200
I'm proud of you, Clark.

00:31:25.200 --> 00:31:27.200
It's who you should have been all along.

00:31:27.200 --> 00:31:30.609
Does that mean you're happy you left?

00:31:30.609 --> 00:31:37.029
It was the hardest decision I have ever had to make.

00:31:37.029 --> 00:31:42.180
But I'm glad that I finally had the guts to do it.

00:31:42.180 --> 00:31:56.089
I would have died before I admitted this.

00:31:56.089 --> 00:32:01.089
But I used to sit on my front porch and look across the field at this far and imagining a summer wedding.

00:32:01.089 --> 00:32:04.750
a summer wedding here.

00:32:04.750 --> 00:32:09.349
Of course, I always thought I'd play a bigger part in it.

00:32:09.349 --> 00:32:12.349
You probably would have if I'd given you Chloe's wedding gift.

00:32:12.349 --> 00:32:24.769
I had Jurelli race all the memories that Chloe had of the real me.

00:32:24.769 --> 00:32:27.769
I wonder if that would have made things different between us.

00:32:27.769 --> 00:32:34.269
I understood the lies that you told me to protect your identity.

00:32:34.269 --> 00:32:37.269
But I could never forgive you for taking that away from me.

00:32:37.269 --> 00:32:39.269
You can't mean that.

00:32:39.269 --> 00:32:42.710
Lana, turned your life upside down.

00:32:42.710 --> 00:32:44.710
Maybe it was exactly what it needed.

00:32:44.710 --> 00:32:53.980
I could have landed a lot of places in my life, Clark, but without you, none of them would have led me here.

00:32:53.980 --> 00:33:11.549
So that's it. It's all over. It's that easy?

00:33:11.549 --> 00:33:19.109
No. But where I am now, for the first time it feels right.

00:33:19.109 --> 00:33:26.690
Clark, I know neither of us could say it.

00:33:26.690 --> 00:33:32.900
But maybe Clark Kent and Lana Lang just weren't meant to end up together.

00:33:32.900 --> 00:34:18.019
Who was that?

00:34:18.019 --> 00:36:58.739
I think took Chloe.

00:36:58.739 --> 00:37:39.219
He's using every satellite in his company to try to track down where that thing might have taken her.

00:37:39.219 --> 00:37:50.460
Clark, there's nothing more you can do for me.

00:37:50.460 --> 00:38:01.039
You don't need to stay.

00:38:01.039 --> 00:38:19.030
I need to find Chloe.

00:38:19.030 --> 00:38:21.030
Jimmy's in bad shape.

00:38:21.030 --> 00:38:24.030
The nurse said they had him stabilized.

00:38:24.030 --> 00:38:26.030
But he's not out of the woods.

00:38:26.030 --> 00:38:28.030
He has severe internal bleeding.

00:38:28.030 --> 00:38:31.030
They're medevacking him to Star City to one of the country's top surgeons.

00:38:31.030 --> 00:38:34.500
I'm going to go with him.

00:38:34.500 --> 00:38:38.840
I'll stay there until I hear from him.

00:38:38.840 --> 00:38:45.639
Why did this have to happen to her?

00:38:45.639 --> 00:38:55.340
Why do these terrible things keep happening all around us?

00:38:55.340 --> 00:38:59.159
Promise. We're going to get Chloe back.

00:38:59.159 --> 00:39:29.170
It's the kind of thing you get when you're not looking.

00:39:29.170 --> 00:39:33.170
It's the kind of thing you had from the start.

